<h1>Configuration</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">.vexesrc format, signal overrides, severity thresholds, ignore patterns, and output settings.</p>

    <h2 id="zero-config">Zero Configuration</h2>

    <p>vexes works with zero configuration. All defaults are designed for security: every signal is enabled, no packages are ignored, and the scanner uses the strictest safe defaults. Configuration is only needed when you want to customize behavior.</p>

    <h2 id="vexesrc">.vexesrc</h2>

    <p>Create a <code>.vexesrc</code> file in your project root for per-project configuration. YAML format.</p>

    <div class="code-block"><span class="cmt"># .vexesrc</span>
<span class="kw">severity</span>: high              <span class="cmt"># minimum severity to report: low, medium, high, critical</span>
<span class="kw">format</span>: text                <span class="cmt"># output format: text, json, sarif</span>

<span class="kw">ecosystems</span>:
  <span class="kw">include</span>:
    - npm
    - cargo                   <span class="cmt"># only scan these ecosystems</span>

<span class="kw">signals</span>:
  <span class="kw">suppress</span>:
    - DORMANT_REACTIVATION    <span class="cmt"># suppress noisy signals</span>
    - PROVENANCE_MISSING
  <span class="kw">override</span>:
    RAPID_RELEASE: low        <span class="cmt"># downgrade severity</span>

<span class="kw">ignore</span>:
  <span class="kw">packages</span>:
    - internal-tool           <span class="cmt"># skip specific packages</span>
  <span class="kw">advisories</span>:
    - GHSA-xxxx-yyyy-zzzz    <span class="cmt"># suppress specific advisories</span></div>

    <h2 id="configuration-options">All Options</h2>

    <table class="cmd-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Key</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>severity</code></td><td><code>low</code></td><td>Minimum severity to report. One of: low, medium, high, critical.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>format</code></td><td><code>text</code></td><td>Output format. One of: text, json, sarif.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ecosystems.include</code></td><td>all</td><td>Array of ecosystem names to scan. If omitted, all detected ecosystems are scanned.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ecosystems.exclude</code></td><td>none</td><td>Array of ecosystem names to skip.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>signals.suppress</code></td><td>none</td><td>Array of signal names to suppress entirely. Undisableable signals cannot be suppressed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>signals.override</code></td><td>none</td><td>Map of signal name to severity. Override the default severity for a signal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ignore.packages</code></td><td>none</td><td>Array of package names to skip during analysis.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ignore.advisories</code></td><td>none</td><td>Array of advisory IDs (GHSA, CVE) to suppress.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="undisableable">Undisableable Signals</h2>

    <p>Four signals cannot be suppressed or severity-overridden via configuration:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><code>KNOWN_COMPROMISED</code></li>
      <li><code>PHANTOM_DEPENDENCY</code></li>
      <li><code>CIRCULAR_STAGING</code></li>
      <li><code>CAPABILITY_ESCALATION</code></li>
    </ul>

    <p>Attempting to add these to <code>signals.suppress</code> will produce a warning and the signals will still be reported. This is a deliberate security design choice -- these signals indicate conditions where suppression is never safe.</p>

    <h2 id="config-merging">Configuration Merging</h2>

    <p>vexes looks for <code>.vexesrc</code> in the current directory, then walks up to the filesystem root. The first <code>.vexesrc</code> found is used. There is no config file merging -- the nearest file wins.</p>

    <h3>Prototype pollution protection</h3>
    <p>Config file merging rejects <code>__proto__</code>, <code>constructor</code>, and <code>prototype</code> keys in YAML. This prevents prototype pollution attacks via malicious config files.</p>

    <h2 id="environment-variables">Environment Variables</h2>

    <p>Configuration can also be set via environment variables. Environment variables take precedence over <code>.vexesrc</code> values.</p>

    <table class="cmd-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Equivalent .vexesrc Key</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>VEXES_SEVERITY</code></td><td><code>severity</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>VEXES_FORMAT</code></td><td><code>format</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>VEXES_ECOSYSTEMS</code></td><td><code>ecosystems.include</code> (comma-separated)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="code-block"><span class="cmt"># Set severity via environment</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">VEXES_SEVERITY=critical vexes scan</span></div>
